2026-11-18T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-2498) 'A ZFS pool written raw to a BDXL disc
 # uuid: 50d1e693-331b-57fa-b210-e85270c9168d
 # tags: rfd:title
 RFD:Discussion  1 RFD
 Serials:VSekaiFabric

2026-11-18T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2498) 'a 100 GB BDXL archive is an encrypted ZFS pool image written to the disc raw.
 # tags: rfd:feature, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2498) 'the encrypted archive image that is written raw to a 100 GB BDXL disc and its contents.
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2498) 'Can a 100 GB BDXL disc hold an encrypted ZFS pool with no filesystem of its own, and how
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2498) 'many bytes of files does that leave room for?
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2498) 'A disc normally carries a UDF filesystem, which takes space and hides the blocks from ZFS.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2498) 'Written raw to a blank disc, the pool image fills the whole raw capacity of about 100.1
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2498) 'billion bytes, and ZFS reads the disc device itself. ZFS still keeps about 3% of the pool
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2498) 'free, so the files get about 96.7 GB.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2498) 'Read the section "Layout and budget" for the measured counts. The check passes when the disc
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2498) 'is read back to the same hash as the image, the pool imports from the disc read-only and
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2498) 'its files match the budget.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2498) 'Layout and budget for a raw BDXL archive
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2498) 'A BDXL archive is one ZFS pool image of 100,103,356,416 bytes with native encryption, written
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2498) 'raw to a blank disc, with one dataset per file set and at most 96,500,000,000 bytes of files.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2498) '- The pool's one disk is a file with the 4096-byte sector shift of RFD66606-2496 (ZFS data
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2498) '  disks). It encrypts with aes-256-gcm and compresses every dataset with zstd.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2498) '- Each file set is one dataset named for the set, and files keep their names and paths.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2498) '- ZFS block checksums replace a separate checksum list. The pool is exported before the
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2498) '  image is written, and the disc is never mounted or formatted.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2498) '- The disc holds one copy of each block, so only a second disc repairs a damaged one.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2498) '- The image size is the disc's raw capacity, a multiple of 4096 bytes. The burn is refused
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2498) '  when the blank disc reports fewer blocks than the image holds.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2498) '- The passphrase is a fresh 24-word BIP39 seed phrase, never a wallet seed. The agent makes
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2498) '  it, pipes it to the pool and stores it in 1Password and the keychain (operator, 2026-11-18).
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2498) '- A file set is stored as an encrypted dataset with its own passphrase on a data pool such
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2498) '  as FIRE202610, and archived by copying it into the disc's pool (operator, 2026-11-18).
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2498) '- An M-DISC BDXL disc counts as the same capacity as a BD-R XL disc until a blank one has
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2498) '  been read in a drive.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2498) '- RFD66606-2496 (ZFS data disks), the pool options this archive inherits.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2498) 'Layout and budget
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2498) 'The raw capacity of a triple-layer BD-R XL disc is 100,103,356,416 bytes, which is
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2498) '48,878,592 logical sectors of 2048 bytes. The figure is listed for BD-R XL and BD-RE XL on
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2498) 'the Wikipedia page for recordable Blu-ray discs, and the multiplication checks out. The
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-2498) 'ISO standard for these discs and the Blu-ray Disc Association paper give only the rounded
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-2498) '100 GB, so the exact figure rests on that page and on burning tools that report real
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-2498) 'discs. A raw write needs no UDF space and no formatting, so the image may use all of it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-2498) 'A disc that was formatted with defect management first would hold 256 MiB less.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:38Z (RFD66606-2498) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:39Z (RFD66606-2498) 'A trial on the Mac made a pool of exactly that size on a file, with OpenZFS 2.3.1 and the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:40Z (RFD66606-2498) 'options below. The pool reported 99,857,989,632 bytes, and the top dataset offered
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:41Z (RFD66606-2498) '96,753,676,288 bytes to files, because ZFS holds back a share of the pool as slop space. A
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:42Z (RFD66606-2498) 'scrub found no errors, and the exported pool imported read-only from the file and loaded its
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:43Z (RFD66606-2498) 'key. The 96,500,000,000-byte budget keeps about 253 MB of that offer in reserve. The trial
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:44Z (RFD66606-2498) 'did not write to a disc, so the raw write and the read from a disc device are untested.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:45Z (RFD66606-2498) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:46Z (RFD66606-2498) 'Making the pool image
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:47Z (RFD66606-2498) 'The options follow RFD66606-2496, with encryption added and a mount point under /Volumes.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:48Z (RFD66606-2498) 'The properties normalization, casesensitivity and utf8only cannot be changed after
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:49Z (RFD66606-2498) 'creation. The trial used a key file in place of the passphrase prompt. Set the four
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:50Z (RFD66606-2498) 'variables first. IMG is an absolute path, because a file disk needs one. The passphrase
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:51Z (RFD66606-2498) 'never goes in a variable: the pool prompts for it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:52Z (RFD66606-2498) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:53Z (RFD66606-2498) '```sh
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:54Z (RFD66606-2498) 'export ZBIN=/usr/local/zfs/bin POOL=NAME SET=<set> IMG=/abs/path/NAME.img
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:55Z (RFD66606-2498) 'truncate -s 100103356416 "$IMG"
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:56Z (RFD66606-2498) 'sudo "$ZBIN/zpool" create -f \
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:57Z (RFD66606-2498) '  -o ashift=12 \
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:58Z (RFD66606-2498) '  -O encryption=aes-256-gcm -O keyformat=passphrase -O keylocation=prompt \
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:00:59Z (RFD66606-2498) '  -O compression=zstd -O atime=off -O copies=1 \
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:00Z (RFD66606-2498) '  -O normalization=formD -O casesensitivity=insensitive -O utf8only=on \
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:01Z (RFD66606-2498) '  -O mountpoint="/Volumes/$POOL" \
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:02Z (RFD66606-2498) '  "$POOL" "$IMG"
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:03Z (RFD66606-2498) 'sudo "$ZBIN/zfs" create "$POOL/$SET"
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:04Z (RFD66606-2498) 'sudo "$ZBIN/zpool" scrub -w "$POOL"
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:05Z (RFD66606-2498) 'sudo "$ZBIN/zpool" export "$POOL"
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:06Z (RFD66606-2498) '```
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:07Z (RFD66606-2498) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:08Z (RFD66606-2498) '- The passphrase reaches the prompt on standard input, so no variable or history line holds
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:09Z (RFD66606-2498) '  it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:10Z (RFD66606-2498) '- The image file is on the internal APFS volume. On the Mac, a file disk on the FIRE202610
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:11Z (RFD66606-2498) '  ZFS pool failed with "no such device in pool", and the same create on APFS ran.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:12Z (RFD66606-2498) '- Autoexpand stays off, so the pool never grows past the image.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:13Z (RFD66606-2498) '- Compression is zstd on the pool and every dataset inherits it. No dataset sets it to off
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:14Z (RFD66606-2498) '  or to another algorithm, because the setting is part of what the checks read back.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:15Z (RFD66606-2498) '- A scrub needs a writable pool, so it runs before the export and not on the disc.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:16Z (RFD66606-2498) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:17Z (RFD66606-2498) 'Store and archive
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:18Z (RFD66606-2498) 'Native encryption is per dataset, so the data pool stays unencrypted and each file set is
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:19Z (RFD66606-2498) 'one encrypted dataset: `zfs create -o encryption=aes-256-gcm -o keyformat=passphrase -o
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:20Z (RFD66606-2498) 'keylocation=prompt POOL/SET`. Names, sizes and properties of datasets stay readable without
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:21Z (RFD66606-2498) 'the key, and file contents, names and paths do not. The archive copies the stored dataset
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:22Z (RFD66606-2498) 'into the disc's pool. Whether a raw `zfs send` keeps the stored key or the disc pool's key
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:23Z (RFD66606-2498) 'governs the copy is untested, so the first archive records which tool was used.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:24Z (RFD66606-2498) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:25Z (RFD66606-2498) 'Writing the disc
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:26Z (RFD66606-2498) 'The first burn tests the write path, so record which tool and flags worked. The candidate on
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:27Z (RFD66606-2498) 'the Mac is `xorriso -as cdrecord`, which writes a raw data track from an image file. Read
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:28Z (RFD66606-2498) 'the blank disc's reported block count first and refuse the burn when it is under
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:29Z (RFD66606-2498) '48,878,592. After the write, read the whole disc back and hash it against the image.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:30Z (RFD66606-2498) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:31Z (RFD66606-2498) 'The passphrase
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:32Z (RFD66606-2498) 'The passphrase is a 24-word BIP39 seed phrase, which carries 256 bits. The agent draws 32
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:33Z (RFD66606-2498) 'random bytes, appends the 8 checksum bits and maps each 11 bits to a word of the list, then
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:34Z (RFD66606-2498) 'stores the phrase in 1Password and the login keychain without printing it. The operator may
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:35Z (RFD66606-2498) 'also keep it on paper apart from the disc. The pool takes the words themselves, lowercase
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:36Z (RFD66606-2498) 'and separated by single spaces, as the passphrase, piped from the keychain to the prompt.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:37Z (RFD66606-2498) 'The pool derives no wallet seed from the words. The word list is the attachment
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:38Z (RFD66606-2498) '`bip39_english.txt` in this RFD's apparatus directory, with its source and license in the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:39Z (RFD66606-2498) '`NOTICE.md` beside it. The agent recomputes the checksum bits from the stored phrase before
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:40Z (RFD66606-2498) 'the pool is made, and reads the keychain and 1Password entries back to the same words.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:41Z (RFD66606-2498) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:42Z (RFD66606-2498) 'Checks
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:43Z (RFD66606-2498) '- Capacity: the blank disc reports at least 48,878,592 blocks, and a blank M-DISC BDXL disc
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:44Z (RFD66606-2498) '  is read in a drive and compared with the raw figure above.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:45Z (RFD66606-2498) '- Compression: `zfs get -r compression NAME` reads zstd on the pool and on every dataset,
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:46Z (RFD66606-2498) '  run before the export.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:47Z (RFD66606-2498) '- Budget: the files total at most 96,500,000,000 bytes, read from the datasets' used space.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:48Z (RFD66606-2498) '- Readback: the whole disc reads back to the same SHA-256 as the image.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:49Z (RFD66606-2498) '- Import: the pool imports from the disc device read-only, the key loads, and the files
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:50Z (RFD66606-2498) '  open.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-18T00:01:51Z (RFD66606-2498) '- Cross host: the same disc imports on Linux and Windows with OpenZFS.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2498  1 LINE
 Text:Written
